## Changes Summary

| File | Change | Reason |
|------|--------|--------|
| **RecentsSection.vue** | Added `setupMessageWatchers()` method with deep watchers on each chat's messages | Force Vue to track nested message changes |
| **RecentsSection.vue** | Added `cleanupMessageWatchers()` in `beforeUnmount` | Prevent memory leaks from unwatched arrays |
| **RecentsSection.vue** | Added `chatMessageWatchers` Map to track active watchers | Avoid duplicate watchers per chat |
| **RecentsSection.vue** | Changed `getUnreadCountReactive()` to read from cache | Triggers re-render when unread counts change |
| **ChatRecentItem.vue** | Added `messageUpdateCounter` data property | Forces computed property re-evaluation |
| **ChatRecentItem.vue** | Added deep watcher on `chat.messages` | Detects nested message array mutations |

This ensures RecentsSection now **reacts identically to ChatSidebar** when the store updates message data.

I'll analyze the code and move the recent chats logic from DesktopSidebar to RecentsSection.

## Analysis

| Component | Current Role | Issue |
|-----------|--------------|-------|
| **DesktopSidebar** | Manages `chats` prop loading, pagination, filtering | Owns data that should belong to RecentsSection |
| **RecentsSection** | Receives `chats` as prop (read-only) | Cannot manage its own data or respond to scroll events |
| **Store (chats.js)** | Has `allChats` getter but no recent-specific logic | Missing recent chat filtering/pagination |

**Problem:** DesktopSidebar loads recent chats but RecentsSection just displays them. This creates a tight coupling and prevents proper reactivity.

**Solution:** Move all recent chat logic to RecentsSection, expose computed properties, and keep DesktopSidebar as a simple container.

