## Analyzing the Bug

Looking at the `loadRecentChats` method carefully, I can spot the issue in the **append logic**:

```js
if (append) {
  this.recentChats.push(...response.chats)
} else {
  this.recentChats = response.chats  // ← Clean assignment on first load
}
```

This looks fine... but the real problem is in **`loadMoreChats`**:

```js
loadMoreChats() {
  if (this.hasMoreChats && !this.isLoading) {
    this.currentPage += 1
    this.loadRecentChats(true)  // ← append = true
  }
},
```

That's also fine. Let me look at `handleScroll`:

```js
handleScroll(e) {
  const { scrollTop, clientHeight, scrollHeight } = e.target
  if (scrollHeight - scrollTop - clientHeight < 100) {
    this.loadMoreChats()  // ← Can be called multiple times rapidly
  }
},
```

---

## The Real Bug — Race Condition / Double Load

The actual problem is more subtle. Look at `mounted()`:

```js
mounted() {
  this.loadRecentChats()   // ← Sets isInitialLoad = true, loads page 1
  this.updateVisibleChats()
},
```

And `loadRecentChats` at the **very beginning**:

```js
async loadRecentChats(append = false) {
  try {
    this.isLoading = true
    const currentUserId = this.currentUser?.id   // ← currentUser might be null here!
```

**`this.currentUser` can be `null/undefined` at mount time** (store not yet populated), so `currentUserId` is `undefined`. The API call goes through with `user_id: undefined`, returns some default/empty/invalid data, and that gets set as `recentChats`.

Then when the store hydrates, nothing re-triggers the load, OR a second load fires and **pushes** onto the contaminated list.

---

## The Specific Invalid Head Item

The `response.chats` likely returns an object like `{ chats: [...] }` but there may be a case where `response` itself is the array, making `response.chats` undefined and:

```js
this.recentChats = response.chats  // undefined
// or
this.recentChats.push(...undefined) // throws, but partially mutated
```

But the **most likely culprit** is this line when `append = true`:

```js
this.recentChats.push(...response.chats)
```

If `response.chats` contains the **same first item** due to an off-by-one in pagination (page overlapping), the duplicate at head would have the same data but be a **different object reference**, causing `v-for :key="chat.id"` conflicts and render failures.

---

## The Fix

```js src/components/layout/RecentsSection.vue
loadMoreChats() {
  if (this.hasMoreChats && !this.isLoading) {
    this.currentPage += 1
    this.isInitialLoad = false  // ← Ensure flag is correct on pagination
    this.loadRecentChats(true)
  }
},
async loadRecentChats(append = false) {
  try {
    this.isLoading = true
    const currentUserId = this.currentUser?.id

    // Guard: don't load without a valid user
    if (!currentUserId) {
      console.warn('RecentsSection: No user ID available, skipping load')
      this.isLoading = false
      return
    }

    const pageSize = this.isInitialLoad ? this.initialPageSize : this.subsequentPageSize

    const response = await this.$project.$api.chats.getRecentChats({
      filters: { user_id: currentUserId },
      page: this.currentPage,
      pageSize: pageSize
    })

    if (response.error) {
      console.error('Error loading recent chats:', response.error)
      this.isLoading = false
      return
    }

    const newChats = (response.chats || []).filter(chat => chat?.id)  // ← Filter invalid items

    if (append) {
      // Deduplicate by id to avoid overlap on page boundaries
      const existingIds = new Set(this.recentChats.map(c => c.id))
      const uniqueNewChats = newChats.filter(c => !existingIds.has(c.id))
      this.recentChats.push(...uniqueNewChats)
    } else {
      this.recentChats = newChats
    }

    this.hasMoreChats = response.has_next
    this.activeChatId = this.$storex?.chats?.activeChat?.id || null
    this.isLoading = false
    this.isInitialLoad = false
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error loading recent chats:', error)
    this.isLoading = false
  }
},
```

### Key fixes:
| Fix | Why |
|-----|-----|
| `if (!currentUserId) return` | Prevents API call with undefined user |
| `.filter(chat => chat?.id)` | Strips any invalid/null items from API response |
| Deduplication by `id` on append | Prevents overlap if page boundaries shift between calls |
| `isInitialLoad = false` in `loadMoreChats` | Ensures correct page size on subsequent loads |

